DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260421T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260421T120000
SUMMARY:Mastering the Art of the Interview
DESCRIPTION:Interviewing can be one of the most difficult aspects of find
 ing a job. Whether you're new to the workforce or changing careers\, prop
 erly preparing yourself ahead of time can boost your confidence\, reduce 
 anxiety and lead to more successful interviews.We'll discuss how and why 
 to research your prospective employer ahead of time and prepare answers t
 o common interview questions. We'll teach you what STAR stories are\, why
  they matter\, and how to create yours. Plus\, we'll cover the importance
  of following up afterward.To request an accommodation\, please contact c
 ap@pcc.edu four days before the event.Meeting Link: https://portlandcc.zo
 om.us/meeting/register/L04VvGxiTsChJJlXq4oFmA#/registration (https://port
 landcc.zoom.us/meeting/register/L04VvGxiTsChJJlXq4oFmA#/registration)—E
 vent Details: https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382581 (https://hub.pcc.edu/rsv
 p?id=382581)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Interviewing can be one of the most difficul
 t aspects of finding a job. Whether you're new to the workforce or changi
 ng careers\, properly preparing yourself ahead of time can boost your con
 fidence\, reduce anxiety and lead to more successful interviews.<br />We'
 ll discuss how and why to research your prospective employer ahead of tim
 e and prepare answers to common interview questions. We'll teach you what
  STAR stories are\, why they matter\, and how to create yours. Plus\, we'
 ll cover the importance of following up afterward.<br />To request an acc
 ommodation\, please contact cap@pcc.edu four days before the event.<br />
